W4A4 Quantization — Inference & Evaluation Release
====================================================

This package is released under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
It builds on several Apache-2.0 open-source projects. Per Apache-2.0 §4, we
retain the upstream attributions below and state the changes we made.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance by component
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. CUDA kernels  (kernels/csrc/)
   Derived from QQQ (https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09904), which is itself
   derived from the Marlin kernel by Elias Frantar (IST-DASLab).
   Attribution chain:  Marlin (Frantar et al.)  ->  QQQ (HandH1998 et al.)  ->  this work.
   The original Marlin/QQQ copyright headers are kept in the source files.
   OUR CHANGES: new W4A4 GEMM kernels (4-bit weights, 4-bit activations) and the
   fused activation quantization/compression path. See "Our contributions" below.

2. Inference layer  (quantize/quant_linear.py)
   The QuantLinearTorch layer that invokes our W4A4 kernel.
   OUR CHANGES: W4A4 forward path (forward_w4a4) and weight packing for our kernel.

3. Quantization / calibration method  (NOT included in this repository)
   The quantized checkpoints evaluated here are produced by the OmniQuant method
   (Shao et al., ICLR 2024, https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.13137). The quantization code
   is not part of this package; see README.md for the quantization configuration.

4. Evaluation harness  (lm_eval/)
   A vendored copy of EleutherAI's lm-evaluation-harness (MIT/Apache-2.0).

